# tier: original-diagnostic
# oracle: independent-derivation
# scenario: diag-stic2-idle-pass
# profile: intv-2609-ntsc-family-p1
# frame: 5 F-M0
# program: fixtures/FX-diag-stic-2/diag-stic-2.listing.txt (ivs-diag-stic-2), entered through the
#   project boot stub contract 2 (boot-stub-2: cartridge reset entry 5000, interrupt entry 5004), with
#   the zero graphics ROM and no EXEC image
#
# Predicate of ivs-diag-stic-2 with no controller input, the idle control (plan 08-07, D-04, D-05, D-10;
# the tier is original-diagnostic because the scenario has no input line by design, the shape lint of the
# playable tier does not apply): the guest words at the one bound (marker 03C5, the frame counter 000A,
# the selector word 00FF, the scene number 0000), frame 0 not displayed, frames 1 and 9 displayed, the
# cards-only picture F-M0 in frame 5 by hash and by five pixel probes, and ten delivered frames, all
# derived by hand in docs/video/diag-stic-2-derivation.md (sections (a) to (f); the frame literal
# data/video/frames/F-M0.frame with its sha256-text key) BEFORE the program, its listing, the scenario or
# any run existed (oracle commit 641a12e3a1059b242cc88a3ee4308e3f58d9b36d, blind second read closed in
# commit 9250265), and copied here line for line from the committed idle block. It was not generated by,
# read back from or edited to match the core or a run. The author of this derivation also wrote the
# literals, the STIC rules, the program and the core, and the blind reader is of the same model family,
# so all of them can share one misreading of a source; agreement among them is not independent evidence
# about hardware.
# Excluded on purpose: machine time (printed in the report, never asserted), the stack word [0340] (C68),
# all CPU registers, R7 and the flags (C40, C45, C56), and every pinned item of the derivation, section
# (i): the pixels of a MOB with the priority bit set (PD-1), half-height pixels (PD-2), a collision of a MOB
# at X coordinate 0 (PD-3), the border bit of a collision register (PD-4), a collision outside the plane
# (PD-5), a collision in a frame with the display off (PD-6), the read and clear semantics of the collision
# registers beyond sticky bits and a write of zero (PD-7), the height unit of the top strip (PD-8), a strip
# against the delay (PD-9), the content of the area a delay exposes and a MOB in it (PD-10, PD-11), the delay
# range (PD-12), and the bus windows against the vertical delay (PD-13).
# Body: one assert per clause in the runner's scenario grammar, hex upper case, exact compare, evaluated
# at the end of the step above it, in the order of data/scenarios/diag-stic2-idle-pass.ivss
# (golden-expect-drift). The step line below is a comment.
# step: run-to 640000 ticks
assert halted == no
assert mem 02F0 == 03C5
assert mem 02F1 == 000A
assert mem 02F2 == 00FF
assert mem 02F3 == 0000
assert frame 0 displayed == no
assert frame 1 displayed == yes
assert frame 9 displayed == yes
assert frame 5 hash == 17df47dfad24a8f419dff876ce3f1d970dd1f0e914b1e8ce3638fbc9904ab39c
assert frame 1 pixel 80 48 == 2
assert frame 9 pixel 84 52 == 2
assert frame 9 pixel 85 52 == 1
assert frame 9 pixel 0 0 == 1
assert frame 9 pixel 158 95 == 1
assert video count == 10
